        {
          "id": "plain-panel-door",
          "status": "canonical",
          "note": "Four- or six-panel, flat or bead profile -- 'trim follows the plain carpenter-stock tradition... does not enter the interior trim family, which stays a board is a board' (trim_family, folk-victorian ancestor)."
        },
        {
          "id": "six-panel-raised-and-fielded",
          "status": "forbidden",
          "note": "Overrides the cascade's inherited value (georgian-colonial-american, via colonial-revival's family). Contradicts the plain, factory-turned-ornament-confined-to-porch-and-cornice discipline this node's own real lineage (folk-victorian) states, and the flat-casing door_surround already correctly bound at this node from the same ancestor."
        }
      ],
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rule": "A plain panel door consistent with the carpenter-stock tradition the coded fabric actually builds in; ornament, where it appears at all, is confined to the porch, cornice, and gable, not the door leaf.",
      "note": "Fixes a cascade bug: the previously-resolved six-panel raised-and-fielded door (via the family splice) is inconsistent with this node's own, correctly-inherited plain door_surround (flat-casing) and trim_family (carpenter-plain-stock)."
